  partName: Engine Block (2)
  description: The Engine Block (2) is the main structural component of the rocket
    engine, located at the middle-center-center, providing a foundation for the cylinders,
    crankshaft, and other critical parts. With a large and complex shape, the engine
    block is designed to withstand the stresses and loads generated by the engine's
    operation, while also serving as a reservoir for engine oil and coolant. Notably,
    the engine block's material is typically a high-strength alloy, allowing it to
    maintain its integrity under extreme conditions.
